{
  "dom_id": "step-q147925",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "The joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint support $S={S}_{X}\\times {S}_{Y}$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $0.1$ | $0.12$ | $0.28$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.2$ | $0.18$ | $0.12$ |\n\nWhich of the following gives the covariance of $X$ and $Y?$",
  "worked_solution": "The covariance of two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint support $S$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])(y-\\text{E}[Y])f(x,y).\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y.$ These are given by the row and column totals, respectively.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=5$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $0.1$ | $0.12$ | $0.28$ | $0.5$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.2$ | $0.18$ | $0.12$ | $0.5$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.3$ | $0.3$ | $0.4$ | $1$ |\n\nWe now compute $\\text{E}[X]$ and $\\text{E}[Y],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0.5+4\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =1+2 \\\\  & =3 \\\\ \\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{Y}}y\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.3+3\\cdot 0.3+5\\cdot 0.4 \\\\  & =0.3+0.9+2 \\\\  & =3.2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for the covariance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-\\text{E}[X])(y-\\text{E}[Y])f(x,y) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}(x-3)(y-3.2)f(x,y).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
